---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";

const canonical = new URL("/about/", Astro.site).toString();
---

<Layout
  title="About MelodyMind Stories"
  description="How MelodyMind Stories researches, writes, sources, and publishes long-form music journalism without analytics, cookies, or saved reader data."
  {canonical}
>
  <article class="about page-shell">
    <header class="about__hero">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">About the publication</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal--second">Music history, with the paperwork left in.</h1>
      <p class="reveal reveal--third">
        MelodyMind Stories follows records, performances, images, and rooms back to the
        sources that document them. The citations are part of the reading experience.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about__body">
      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">Editorial method</p>
        <h2>Claims stay close to evidence.</h2>
        <p>
          Each story begins with museum records, archives, institutional histories, or
          other named sources. When accounts disagree, the article describes the
          disagreement. Direct quotations are used only when a traceable source and a
          clear editorial reason justify them. Song lyrics are not reproduced.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">AI disclosure</p>
        <h2>Assistance is named, not hidden.</h2>
        <p>
          Research and drafting are assisted by AI. The published story includes its
          sources, access dates, image rights, and alteration notes so readers can inspect
          the record behind the prose. MelodyMind Editorial is responsible for the final
          selection, structure, and wording.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h2>Reading leaves no profile here.</h2>
        <p>
          This static site has no accounts, analytics, advertising trackers, cookies,
          external embeds, or client-side storage. The annotated artifact uses a small
          local script to synchronize visible notes; it does not send or save data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">Image rights</p>
        <h2>Every picture carries its catalog note.</h2>
        <p>
          Images are served locally and optimized during the build. Captions name the
          creator, source, license, and any crop or tonal adjustment. The launch edition
          is noncommercial, including its use of material licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="about__footer">
      <a class="text-link" href="/">Read the launch edition <span>→</span></a>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://melody-mind.de/"
        >Visit MelodyMind Music <span>→</span></a
      >
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4xl);
    padding-block: var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .about__hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    max-inline-size: 76rem;
  }

  .about__hero h1 {
    max-inline-size: 15ch;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
  }

  .about__hero > p:last-child {
    max-inline-size: 62ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.18rem, 2.2vw, 1.5rem);
    color: var(--quiet-ink);
  }

  .about__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .about__body section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-xl);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .about__body h2 {
    max-inline-size: 16ch;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .about__body section > p:last-child {
    max-inline-size: 65ch;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: var(--quiet-ink);
  }

  .about__footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-md) var(--space-2xl);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-2xl);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  @media (width >= 64rem) {
    .about__body {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
